            "merged_at": null
          },
          "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes the two digit-recognition/decoding mismatches reported in #1806.\n\n- Correct the `fullwide` decoder range so full-width `８` and `９` are decoded instead of being dropped.\n- Remove the literal `|` from the `hanidec` character class so a pipe is rejected as an unparsable digit input.\n\nThe change is limited to `src/impl/digits.js` and regression coverage in `test/impl/digits.test.js`. It does not broaden the parsing architecture or refactor `parseDigits()`.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `TZ=America/New_York LANG=en_US.utf8 npm run jest -- --runInBand test/impl/digits.test.js` — 5 passed\n- `TZ=America/New_York LANG=en_US.utf8 npm run jest -- --runInBand test/impl/digits.test.js test/datetime/tokenParse.test.js test/duration/create.test.js` — 93 passed\n- `TZ=America/New_York LANG=en_US.utf8 npm run test -- --runInBand` — 59 suites and 1227 tests passed\n- `npm run format-check` — passed\n- `npm run build-node` — passed\n\nThe regression tests exercise all ten fullwide and hanidec digits, all 21 supported numbering systems, normal date and duration parsing, invalid characters, and invalid-input error propagation.\n\nCloses #1806\n\nAI disclosure: Implemented with MiniMax Code CLI 0.5.2, MiniMax-M3.1 (max), independently reviewed and tested by Codex.\n",
